Multiple-role permission resolution
Ito ang recommended precedence:
Account and membership security.
Company isolation.
Non-overridable system restrictions.
Explicit user-specific DENY.
Role grants and compatible role combinations.
Explicit user-specific GRANT, if permitted by the administrator's delegation authority.
Data scope and workflow validation.
Important rules:
Multiple compatible role grants can be combined.
A user-specific DENY must not be bypassed by another role's grant.
A user-specific GRANT cannot bypass SoD, immutable records, or company isolation.
Approval limits must not be added together. Use the most restrictive applicable limit.
Data scopes must be intersected where necessary to prevent wider access from being accidentally granted.
A prohibited role combination must never be resolved through simple permission union.
